WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.844 --> 00:00:03.877
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:03.877 --> 00:00:04.710
It's Evan.

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.779
My one word is "believe" and I believe

00:00:06.779 --> 00:00:09.118
that you have something
special to offer and I'd love

00:00:09.118 --> 00:00:12.729
to see it explode so that you
can help change the planet.

00:00:12.729 --> 00:00:14.192
So to help you on your journey today

00:00:14.192 --> 00:00:15.924
we're going to look at
seven different ways

00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:18.786
that you can make business alliances.

00:00:18.786 --> 00:00:19.992
- [Robotic Voice] Nine...

00:00:19.992 --> 00:00:20.825
Eight...

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:23.255
[Upbeat Music]

00:00:26.808 --> 00:00:28.372
- So one of the fastest
ways to grow your company

00:00:28.372 --> 00:00:29.638
is through alliances.

00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:31.106
You find people who are already selling

00:00:31.106 --> 00:00:33.225
to your target market and instead of you

00:00:33.225 --> 00:00:35.001
having to go one, by one, by one, by one,

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:38.028
talking to potential customers
you want to be able to talk

00:00:38.028 --> 00:00:41.706
to one person, who then
could open you up to tens,

00:00:41.706 --> 00:00:44.998
hundreds, thousands, hundreds
of thousands of customers.

00:00:44.998 --> 00:00:46.238
And so today I'm going to talk about

00:00:46.238 --> 00:00:48.889
seven different ways
to be able to do that.

00:00:48.889 --> 00:00:49.972
[Upbeat Riff]

00:00:51.632 --> 00:00:54.148
Way number one is to look
at where do people buy

00:00:54.148 --> 00:00:55.671
before they buy from you?

00:00:55.671 --> 00:00:58.500
So understand that buying is a cycle.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.526
People are not always
ready to buy from you.

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:01.753
People are not always ready to buy

00:01:01.753 --> 00:01:04.650
from you potential alliance
partners and there's a phase

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.345
where you buy one thing from somebody

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:08.333
and then you graduate
and buy the next thing,

00:01:08.333 --> 00:01:10.353
and buy the next thing and
so what you want to look at

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:12.513
is wherever you are in that buying cycle,

00:01:12.513 --> 00:01:14.943
you want to find all the
people that your customers

00:01:14.943 --> 00:01:17.595
are buying from before they buy from you.

00:01:17.595 --> 00:01:20.564
So as an example, if you
are a graphic designer.

00:01:20.564 --> 00:01:22.036
You know, you're a graphic designer

00:01:22.036 --> 00:01:24.661
and you want to figure
out the buying cycle.

00:01:24.661 --> 00:01:28.339
Maybe before somebody buys
graphic design services,

00:01:28.339 --> 00:01:32.084
they have built a website
or they've got hosting,

00:01:32.084 --> 00:01:35.016
or they've just incorporated a business

00:01:35.016 --> 00:01:36.947
and so all of those people here,

00:01:36.947 --> 00:01:38.677
you want to start making connections with.

00:01:38.677 --> 00:01:39.871
You want to take them out for lunch,

00:01:39.871 --> 00:01:41.634
you want to approach them, grab a coffee,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.872
understand them and you want
to learn about their business

00:01:44.872 --> 00:01:47.068
and it's way easier to set up a meeting

00:01:47.068 --> 00:01:49.494
with a potential partner because
you can help each other out

00:01:49.494 --> 00:01:52.189
much more that it is to make a cold call

00:01:52.189 --> 00:01:54.384
and try to get a meeting with a customer.

00:01:54.384 --> 00:01:56.205
And so I'm trying to
understand these people.

00:01:56.205 --> 00:01:58.651
I'm trying to figure
out how I can help them.

00:01:58.651 --> 00:02:00.639
If you get business that you

00:02:00.639 --> 00:02:03.057
could potentially give to
them, that's great, right?

00:02:03.057 --> 00:02:05.887
If you now know somebody
that needs website design,

00:02:05.887 --> 00:02:09.184
or needs hosting or business
set up, you could refer them

00:02:09.184 --> 00:02:11.096
to these people and also you're hoping

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:12.487
that if you make a good impression,

00:02:12.487 --> 00:02:14.610
they could refer business onto you.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.152
And understand that sometimes
you need to work out

00:02:17.152 --> 00:02:19.558
a relationship with a
commission or a fee structure

00:02:19.558 --> 00:02:23.253
where they get a flat amount
in they refer you a client,

00:02:23.253 --> 00:02:25.424
or they get a percentage of a deal

00:02:25.424 --> 00:02:26.641
if they refer you a client.

00:02:26.641 --> 00:02:28.020
A lot of times they do this just because

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.689
it makes them look good.

00:02:29.689 --> 00:02:31.484
It's a value added service.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:34.569
If I'm a web hosting company,
and I've just taken on

00:02:34.569 --> 00:02:36.374
a new client and I know
they need graphic design,

00:02:36.374 --> 00:02:40.055
if I introduce them to
somebody who does a great job,

00:02:40.055 --> 00:02:41.571
it makes them look good.

00:02:41.571 --> 00:02:44.238
So if you do a great job for your clients,

00:02:44.238 --> 00:02:45.609
anybody that's been referred in,

00:02:45.609 --> 00:02:48.242
it actually makes that
person look great as well

00:02:48.242 --> 00:02:50.612
and you're going to get a lot
more deals coming through.

00:02:50.612 --> 00:02:53.132
So understand who the
people are that your clients

00:02:53.132 --> 00:02:56.289
are buying from before
they ever buy from you.

00:02:56.289 --> 00:02:57.575
Get to know them, take them to coffee,

00:02:57.575 --> 00:02:58.780
understand their business and try

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.641
to find a way to work together.

00:03:00.641 --> 00:03:01.724
[Upbeat Riff]

00:03:03.827 --> 00:03:05.433
Way number two is to
understand where people

00:03:05.433 --> 00:03:07.188
buy from after they buy from you.

00:03:07.188 --> 00:03:09.159
So, we understand where
they're buying from before,

00:03:09.159 --> 00:03:10.548
obviously then they're buying from us.

00:03:10.548 --> 00:03:11.461
What's next?

00:03:11.461 --> 00:03:12.840
Who is out in this range?

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:15.607
So if I'm a graphic designer,
and I'm making people

00:03:15.607 --> 00:03:17.831
a beautiful business
card, well what's next?

00:03:17.831 --> 00:03:19.116
They're going to need a printer.

00:03:19.116 --> 00:03:19.949
So what I'm going to do now

00:03:19.949 --> 00:03:21.162
is go and meet all of these people,

00:03:21.162 --> 00:03:22.892
because these are all
potential alliance partners

00:03:22.892 --> 00:03:24.189
for my business as well.

00:03:24.189 --> 00:03:26.000
I want to talk to all
the printers in my area.

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.523
I want to talk to
anybody who they're gunna

00:03:27.523 --> 00:03:29.379
then take my graphic design services

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:31.879
and do the next step with.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:33.448
I want to talk to those
people cause again,

00:03:33.448 --> 00:03:35.932
one, it's easy to make those meetings

00:03:35.932 --> 00:03:37.593
cause those partnerships
you could potentially

00:03:37.593 --> 00:03:39.080
help both of each other out.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:41.616
It gives you a path to
refer your clients onto,

00:03:41.616 --> 00:03:43.661
and then if clients are
going to them and saying

00:03:43.661 --> 00:03:46.431
"hey I love your printing
services, but before we use you

00:03:46.431 --> 00:03:49.913
we need to get a good graphic
design concept completed

00:03:49.913 --> 00:03:51.083
for our business card," right?

00:03:51.083 --> 00:03:53.296
They could then pass it onto you, right?

00:03:53.296 --> 00:03:55.980
And if you do a good job
then you make them look good.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.328
So again the same idea of
do you want to give them

00:03:58.328 --> 00:04:00.574
a commission, a flat fee or just be able

00:04:00.574 --> 00:04:02.065
to pass those frills
back and forth and have

00:04:02.065 --> 00:04:03.863
that kind of trusted relationship.

00:04:03.863 --> 00:04:06.636
Meeting with people on
both sides of the equation,

00:04:06.636 --> 00:04:08.481
and forming as many
partnerships as you can

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.666
can really help explode your customer base

00:04:10.666 --> 00:04:13.728
much faster than going after
customers one at a time.

00:04:13.728 --> 00:04:14.811
[Upbeat Riff]

00:04:17.126 --> 00:04:18.444
Way number three to make alliances

00:04:18.444 --> 00:04:19.660
is through your customers.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.845
A lot of times your customers
can be great conduits

00:04:22.845 --> 00:04:25.902
for either becoming a business
partner in your company,

00:04:25.902 --> 00:04:27.724
passing referrals onto you,

00:04:27.724 --> 00:04:29.770
doing a tighter kind of integration with.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:31.545
In my first software company,

00:04:31.545 --> 00:04:35.391
we always used our customers
to fund our next development.

00:04:35.391 --> 00:04:38.395
So we had our base software,
and then if a customer wanted

00:04:38.395 --> 00:04:41.578
a custom feature built, we
would charge them for it.

00:04:41.578 --> 00:04:42.823
Like, okay, you want that thing added?

00:04:42.823 --> 00:04:44.534
Great, we can do it and
it's going to cost you

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:45.631
this amount of money.

00:04:45.631 --> 00:04:46.739
We would do it at cost.

00:04:46.739 --> 00:04:48.136
We wouldn't really make a ton of profit

00:04:48.136 --> 00:04:50.225
off of that development,
but then that feeds into

00:04:50.225 --> 00:04:52.309
our product and we can sell to everybody

00:04:52.309 --> 00:04:53.994
and so any time any customers wanted

00:04:53.994 --> 00:04:56.452
that custom integration,
custom development,

00:04:56.452 --> 00:04:59.515
we would do it and it
helps everybody else.

00:04:59.515 --> 00:05:01.853
So they're helping fund
our business to grow.

00:05:01.853 --> 00:05:03.493
On my YouTube channel, as an example.

00:05:03.493 --> 00:05:05.534
When I wanted to promote
my book, we reached out

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.313
to a number of you guys
that had YouTube channels

00:05:07.313 --> 00:05:08.945
that were already a part of the community.

00:05:08.945 --> 00:05:10.976
You guys are my customers and we're doing

00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:12.811
some business development with and see

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.636
how we can help each
other out and I appeared

00:05:14.636 --> 00:05:16.364
on your channel, you
appeared on my channels

00:05:16.364 --> 00:05:18.728
and so there's a lot of
ways to make it work.

00:05:18.728 --> 00:05:21.456
If I look at at Toronto
Dance Salsa as an example,

00:05:21.456 --> 00:05:23.461
we look at the companies
that people work at

00:05:23.461 --> 00:05:26.493
and often the students
who come in then take

00:05:26.493 --> 00:05:28.611
the message back to their
company and they tell

00:05:28.611 --> 00:05:30.429
their friends and they might put up a sign

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:33.810
in the lunch area and
help promote the school

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:36.202
and talk about us on
social media, you know,

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:38.227
so you want to basically get as close

00:05:38.227 --> 00:05:39.714
to your customers as possible.

00:05:39.714 --> 00:05:41.896
You want to understand
why they came to you,

00:05:41.896 --> 00:05:43.774
what their needs are,
what they do for a living,

00:05:43.774 --> 00:05:45.948
what makes them tick, what
their needs, passions,

00:05:45.948 --> 00:05:49.154
desires are and one: that just helps you

00:05:49.154 --> 00:05:51.323
get more referrals, right?

00:05:51.323 --> 00:05:53.030
If they know you, like you, trust you,

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:54.260
they might tell their friends about you

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:57.219
but it could also lead
to a greater integration

00:05:57.219 --> 00:05:58.511
with what they're doing.

00:05:58.511 --> 00:05:59.994
It may lead to a tighter relationship

00:05:59.994 --> 00:06:01.277
with the business that they're at.

00:06:01.277 --> 00:06:02.701
More sales, more orders.

00:06:02.701 --> 00:06:04.282
Introductions up the line.

00:06:04.282 --> 00:06:07.037
When I had my software
company, another quick example.

00:06:07.037 --> 00:06:09.269
So we got one scientist
at Johnson and Johnson

00:06:09.269 --> 00:06:10.960
to buy our software.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:12.457
Johnson and Johnson's a huge company.

00:06:12.457 --> 00:06:14.767
They have tons of scientists
and so we want to really

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.408
get to know that person and
see how can we use that person

00:06:17.408 --> 00:06:20.421
to get introductions to
the other scientists?

00:06:20.421 --> 00:06:22.108
And then you get all the
scientists in that one area.

00:06:22.108 --> 00:06:25.744
Then how do you use those guys
to leap frog to another area

00:06:25.744 --> 00:06:27.760
and so soon you're getting
more and more and more

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:29.300
and more and more of the company.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.899
Now you can't do that with every customer

00:06:30.899 --> 00:06:32.215
but the more you understand

00:06:32.215 --> 00:06:33.962
each individual customer you have,

00:06:33.962 --> 00:06:35.270
then you can try to figure out

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:37.205
is there any kind of
relationship that we can have

00:06:37.205 --> 00:06:39.223
to help grow this business together?

00:06:39.223 --> 00:06:40.306
[Upbeat Riff]

00:06:42.435 --> 00:06:44.869
- Tip number four is to use social media.

00:06:44.869 --> 00:06:48.148
So I wanted to build a list of
potential alliance partners.

00:06:48.148 --> 00:06:50.341
The first thing I did was
to reach out to people

00:06:50.341 --> 00:06:52.300
who are already familiar with me.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:55.481
I have a series called
"Unlocking Lily" on this channel.

00:06:55.481 --> 00:06:57.914
I reached out to people who
are commenting on my videos

00:06:57.914 --> 00:07:00.365
to do possible collaborations.

00:07:00.365 --> 00:07:02.609
The second thing I did
was to reach out to people

00:07:02.609 --> 00:07:04.089
who have reviewed Evan's book

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:06.199
or interviewed him on their channel.

00:07:06.199 --> 00:07:09.000
That way we have a
mutual interest as well.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.028
And the third thing that
I did was to go through

00:07:11.028 --> 00:07:14.218
Evan's videos and to read
the comments of the people.

00:07:14.218 --> 00:07:15.942
And there I looked at people's comments

00:07:15.942 --> 00:07:18.673
that resonated with me and
I looked at their channel.

00:07:18.673 --> 00:07:20.383
If they had an "About"
page I looked at what

00:07:20.383 --> 00:07:22.938
they were about to see if
we align with our mission

00:07:22.938 --> 00:07:24.717
and we could work well together.

00:07:24.717 --> 00:07:28.111
From there I was able to create
my list of a thousand names

00:07:28.111 --> 00:07:29.945
and I had some great collaborations

00:07:29.945 --> 00:07:32.766
and even out of that I
made some great friends.

00:07:32.766 --> 00:07:35.375
So to build alliances on social media,

00:07:35.375 --> 00:07:38.454
the number one thing you want
to do is create a big list.

00:07:38.454 --> 00:07:40.101
Mine was a thousand.

00:07:40.101 --> 00:07:43.381
The more names you have, the
more possibilities you'll have.

00:07:43.381 --> 00:07:46.422
Number two is to find
people that already know you

00:07:46.422 --> 00:07:48.410
and who are already following you

00:07:48.410 --> 00:07:50.645
and number three is to find people

00:07:50.645 --> 00:07:52.526
who have similar interest as you.

00:07:52.526 --> 00:07:54.446
If there's certain videos
that you love to watch,

00:07:54.446 --> 00:07:55.995
look at the people commenting.

00:07:55.995 --> 00:07:58.165
Chances are they're on
the same mission as you.

00:07:58.165 --> 00:07:59.248
[Upbeat Riff]

00:08:01.751 --> 00:08:04.496
- The number five way is
though your suppliers.

00:08:04.496 --> 00:08:05.501
Think about all the people

00:08:05.501 --> 00:08:07.261
who you are currently spending money with.

00:08:07.261 --> 00:08:09.967
People who you are paying
on a regular basis,

00:08:09.967 --> 00:08:11.894
whether you're buying a
product or service from them,

00:08:11.894 --> 00:08:14.563
and see if there might be a
way that they could help make

00:08:14.563 --> 00:08:16.376
introductions for you to other people

00:08:16.376 --> 00:08:17.711
that might help your business.

00:08:17.711 --> 00:08:19.933
So an easiest case example is looking

00:08:19.933 --> 00:08:23.125
at lawyers, accountants, bookkeepers.

00:08:23.125 --> 00:08:25.127
These are people who deal with

00:08:25.127 --> 00:08:26.427
a lot of different entrepreneurs.

00:08:26.427 --> 00:08:28.289
A lot of different kinds of businesses.

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:30.008
And so if they know what
your business is about

00:08:30.008 --> 00:08:31.672
and they know the kinds of partnerships

00:08:31.672 --> 00:08:34.306
that you're looking to make,
just letting them know.

00:08:34.306 --> 00:08:35.967
You know, this is somebody
who you might be paying

00:08:35.967 --> 00:08:39.016
once a quarter, maybe once a year.

00:08:39.016 --> 00:08:41.012
Maybe more frequently if
you have more business,

00:08:41.012 --> 00:08:42.652
but they have a vested interest

00:08:42.652 --> 00:08:45.191
in helping their clients come together

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:48.035
and form greater relationships
because if you do that

00:08:48.035 --> 00:08:49.912
then they're going to
make more business, right?

00:08:49.912 --> 00:08:50.753
Like, you're going to come back.

00:08:50.753 --> 00:08:51.687
You're going to give them referrals.

00:08:51.687 --> 00:08:55.270
If you're looking at people
that you buy supplies from.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:57.704
You know, if you're
buying t-shirts from them

00:08:57.704 --> 00:09:00.146
and you're putting a big order
every month to buy t-shirts,

00:09:00.146 --> 00:09:02.308
is there anybody that they may know

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:04.527
that could potentially help your business?

00:09:04.527 --> 00:09:06.326
Like what is the kind
of alliance partnership

00:09:06.326 --> 00:09:08.207
that you're looking for in an ideal world

00:09:08.207 --> 00:09:11.409
and do they have somebody that
they could introduce you to?

00:09:11.409 --> 00:09:13.813
And so it doesn't hurt to make
a list of all your suppliers.

00:09:13.813 --> 00:09:15.024
All the people that you're
spending money with.

00:09:15.024 --> 00:09:18.951
Now, if you're spending thirty
bucks a month on, you know,

00:09:18.951 --> 00:09:22.290
Verizon to get internet,
I'm sure they're not going

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:23.925
to really care about helping you out.

00:09:23.925 --> 00:09:25.800
And so the easier ones
that when you're dealing

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.412
with a person, you know, an entrepreneur,

00:09:28.412 --> 00:09:31.269
or a physical sales person at a company

00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:33.187
and you have a relationship with them.

00:09:33.187 --> 00:09:34.810
Learn to tighten that relationship.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:35.643
Get to know them.

00:09:35.643 --> 00:09:36.476
Take them to coffee.

00:09:36.476 --> 00:09:37.426
Have a lunch with them.

00:09:37.426 --> 00:09:38.844
Understand what they're after to.

00:09:38.844 --> 00:09:39.677
And try to figure out how you might

00:09:39.677 --> 00:09:41.187
be able to help each other out.

00:09:41.187 --> 00:09:44.004
Suppliers can be a fantastic
alliance partnership for you.

00:09:44.004 --> 00:09:45.087
[Upbeat Riff]

00:09:47.101 --> 00:09:49.516
Way number six is through
banks and governments.

00:09:49.516 --> 00:09:50.349
And I put these two together

00:09:50.349 --> 00:09:54.714
because they're both
low leverage typically

00:09:54.714 --> 00:09:56.677
but it really just depends on the person.

00:09:56.677 --> 00:09:58.582
And so when I first just
got started in my business,

00:09:58.582 --> 00:10:01.751
I went to the bank and I said
"hey, I'd like some help."

00:10:01.751 --> 00:10:03.678
And he said "well do you need a loan?"

00:10:03.678 --> 00:10:05.349
Uh, I dunno if I need a loan.

00:10:05.349 --> 00:10:06.867
I just got started.

00:10:06.867 --> 00:10:07.857
I don't know what I'm doing.

00:10:07.857 --> 00:10:08.865
I need help.

00:10:08.865 --> 00:10:13.223
So that's not what banks really
do but it was with somebody

00:10:13.223 --> 00:10:15.820
who was nice enough to then
put me on to somebody else

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:18.783
who then became one of my
first mentors in my business.

00:10:18.783 --> 00:10:21.153
So again, banks see people all day long

00:10:21.153 --> 00:10:24.666
who are potentially able to
make connections for you.

00:10:24.666 --> 00:10:26.671
A lot of people don't
even know their banker.

00:10:26.671 --> 00:10:28.535
It's a good idea just in
general to get to know

00:10:28.535 --> 00:10:30.865
who your banker is cause
if you ever need money,

00:10:30.865 --> 00:10:34.069
if you're ever trying to get
any kind of debt facility,

00:10:34.069 --> 00:10:36.384
that personal connection
makes a big difference

00:10:36.384 --> 00:10:38.156
but they may also be able to refer you

00:10:38.156 --> 00:10:40.246
to other clients that they have.

00:10:40.246 --> 00:10:42.493
Again, it really depends
on the individual.

00:10:42.493 --> 00:10:44.719
Sometimes individual
bankers are really friendly

00:10:44.719 --> 00:10:46.652
and really customer
focused and really driven

00:10:46.652 --> 00:10:48.444
to help their clients succeed.

00:10:48.444 --> 00:10:51.193
Other times bankers just
want to climb the ladder,

00:10:51.193 --> 00:10:53.482
they hate this job, they want
to move up to the next step.

00:10:53.482 --> 00:10:55.085
They don't really care
about their clients.

00:10:55.085 --> 00:10:57.301
And so it makes it harder
to form that relationship.

00:10:57.301 --> 00:10:59.520
Government, on the other
hand, a lot of governments

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:00.900
have different programs in place.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.122
In Toronto, as an example,
we have a group called

00:11:03.122 --> 00:11:04.079
"Enterprise Toronto."

00:11:04.079 --> 00:11:05.157
It's funded by the city.

00:11:05.157 --> 00:11:07.757
It has multiple locations
here and you can walk in

00:11:07.757 --> 00:11:09.296
and get help with your business.

00:11:09.296 --> 00:11:11.707
They have advisors who
try to give you feedback.

00:11:11.707 --> 00:11:13.563
They will help assess your business plan.

00:11:13.563 --> 00:11:16.474
They have multiple different
programs where you can apply

00:11:16.474 --> 00:11:18.588
for funding and different opportunities

00:11:18.588 --> 00:11:20.612
but they also try to connect you together.

00:11:20.612 --> 00:11:22.557
You get to know the resource manager.

00:11:22.557 --> 00:11:25.268
At Enterprise Toronto,
they may have mentors

00:11:25.268 --> 00:11:27.053
they can connect you to, they may remember

00:11:27.053 --> 00:11:29.422
another entrepreneur
that came in last week

00:11:29.422 --> 00:11:31.303
that might be a good potential fit for you

00:11:31.303 --> 00:11:35.064
and so it really depends on
what's happening in your city.

00:11:35.064 --> 00:11:36.514
You may be fortunate enough to have a lot

00:11:36.514 --> 00:11:38.056
of good government programs.

00:11:38.056 --> 00:11:39.144
You may have nothing.

00:11:39.144 --> 00:11:40.590
So that may not be a path for you.

00:11:40.590 --> 00:11:42.220
So put banks and government together

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:45.392
because it really depends
on the circumstances

00:11:45.392 --> 00:11:47.566
and who you end up being
able to connect with

00:11:47.566 --> 00:11:49.594
but it's at least worth
exploring to see if there's

00:11:49.594 --> 00:11:52.232
an opportunity for you to
make an alliance partnership.

00:11:52.232 --> 00:11:53.315
[Upbeat Riff]

00:11:55.660 --> 00:11:58.492
And number seven, my last way
to form alliance partnerships,

00:11:58.492 --> 00:11:59.764
is through targeted events.

00:11:59.764 --> 00:12:04.128
I'd be looking at where my
ideal partners are hanging out.

00:12:04.128 --> 00:12:05.510
What kind of events they're going to

00:12:05.510 --> 00:12:08.211
and go to those events
to get to know people.

00:12:08.211 --> 00:12:11.587
So if you're looking at making
a partnership with people

00:12:11.587 --> 00:12:15.072
who are, you know, techies who
are really into programming.

00:12:15.072 --> 00:12:17.550
You want to have a custom development shop

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.509
as an alliance partner,
then you want to hang out

00:12:20.509 --> 00:12:21.585
at the events that they care about.

00:12:21.585 --> 00:12:23.950
Even if it's not super
relevant to you, right?

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.249
Like, you may not care
anything about programming

00:12:26.249 --> 00:12:27.905
and the latest PHP development

00:12:27.905 --> 00:12:29.795
and all the stuff that's coming out.

00:12:29.795 --> 00:12:31.584
You don't care about that, but they do,

00:12:31.584 --> 00:12:33.356
and they're hanging out there so you want

00:12:33.356 --> 00:12:34.814
to go there and get to know them.

00:12:34.814 --> 00:12:37.828
Whether that's a conference,
whether that's a meet up group,

00:12:37.828 --> 00:12:39.562
whether that's some local
event that's happening

00:12:39.562 --> 00:12:42.112
in your city, if you know
your target partners...

00:12:42.112 --> 00:12:43.364
This is marketing 101.

00:12:43.364 --> 00:12:46.573
If you know your target
partners are gunna be there,

00:12:46.573 --> 00:12:49.396
you want to be there to get to know them.

00:12:49.396 --> 00:12:51.558
And the advantage is of you being there

00:12:51.558 --> 00:12:54.229
is a lot of times the
people who are like you,

00:12:54.229 --> 00:12:57.096
your competition, is not gunna be there.

00:12:57.096 --> 00:13:00.464
The people who are gunna be
there are more people like them.

00:13:00.464 --> 00:13:03.242
Their competitors, who
may not want to talk to

00:13:03.242 --> 00:13:06.647
and do deals with, but this
outsider comes in promoting

00:13:06.647 --> 00:13:09.653
this different option that
is potentially complimentary

00:13:09.653 --> 00:13:13.352
to them, you stand out
in the sea of similarness

00:13:13.352 --> 00:13:15.190
and people will want to talk to you

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:17.093
and it's a competitive advantage.

00:13:17.093 --> 00:13:18.524
Versus where you might go.

00:13:18.524 --> 00:13:20.565
If you're a marketer, you
might go to marketing events.

00:13:20.565 --> 00:13:22.048
You're like everyone else there.

00:13:22.048 --> 00:13:25.515
If the programmer came there,
he would have an easier time

00:13:25.515 --> 00:13:28.924
making those connections and
so hanging out is for talking

00:13:28.924 --> 00:13:31.377
to customers too, but
hanging out where the people

00:13:31.377 --> 00:13:34.459
who you want to talk to
are, even if it's outside

00:13:34.459 --> 00:13:36.443
your comfort zone or where
you would normally go

00:13:36.443 --> 00:13:38.095
is super important because that's how

00:13:38.095 --> 00:13:39.502
you're gunna get the connections.

00:13:39.502 --> 00:13:40.632
So those are my seven tips

00:13:40.632 --> 00:13:42.375
on how to form alliance partnerships.

00:13:42.375 --> 00:13:45.155
Again, forming alliances
is one of the fastest ways

00:13:45.155 --> 00:13:46.885
to grow your company
because you're thinking

00:13:46.885 --> 00:13:49.791
"I want to target one
person, or ten people,

00:13:49.791 --> 00:13:52.002
or a group of people who
then could introduce me

00:13:52.002 --> 00:13:53.937
to tons of people."

00:13:53.937 --> 00:13:56.509
The goal is not to go after
one customer, one customer,

00:13:56.509 --> 00:13:58.089
one customer at a time.

00:13:58.089 --> 00:14:01.236
It works but it's not very
efficient of effective.

00:14:01.236 --> 00:14:03.101
Where if you talk to the
people who could make multiple

00:14:03.101 --> 00:14:05.315
introductions for you,
you're much more likely

00:14:05.315 --> 00:14:08.056
to hyper explode your business.

00:14:08.056 --> 00:14:09.572
So I'd love to know what you think.

